    {
      "did": "did:plc:ty33p3ngkm6wvna6lgfvcgnj",
      "time_us": 1795284552353002,
      "cursor": 27436904678,
      "kind": "commit",
      "commit": {
        "rev": "3n2tp32426x22",
        "operation": "create",
        "collection": "org.tangled.track.ticket",
        "rkey": "17",
        "record": {
          "$type": "org.tangled.track.ticket",
          "body": {
            "$type": "org.tangled.markup.markdown",
            "text": "tg and current Tangled clients find a spindle through its did:web DID and talk to it over `org.tangled.*`. Loom's embedded core v1.16 served neither: `/.well-known/did.json`, `org.tangled.spindle.describeSpindle` and `org.tangled.ci.*` all returned 404, so tg couldn't reach CI on loom.jarrett.net. Core v1.20.1 serves all of them.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Dependency:** core >= v1.20.0 can't be fetched as a Go module, because fixture paths with `:` in them break the module zip. `tangled.org/core` is replaced with `tangled.org/evan.jarrett.net/core v1.20.1-loom.1`, which is upstream v1.20.1 plus a `localinfra/fixtures/go.mod`. Drop the replace once upstream takes that fix (branch `fixtures-gomod` on the core fork).\n- **Code:** the engine, controller and `main.go` are ported to the v1.20 API. `PipelineId` is now a TID minted by the spindle. `main` sets up the quota manager, migrates pre-v1.20 log files, and releases reservations recovered from an interrupted run.\n- **Image:** v1.20 links hydrant (Rust) through cgo. A new Dockerfile stage builds `libhydrant_ffi.a` from the hydrant version `go.mod` pins. Go builder images are bumped to 1.26.\n- **Deployment:** Helm and kustomize gain the signing key Secret mount, `SPINDLE_CONTACT_EMAIL`, the hydrant dir on the spindle PVC, and admission/admins values. The dead tap setting is removed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make test` and `make lint` pass, as do `helm lint` and `kubectl kustomize config/default`.\n- The amd64 image ran against envtest: `did.json`, `describeSpindle`, `org.tangled.ci.queryPipelines` and `/_health` answer, and hydrant reached plc.directory.\n- arm64: hydrant and the controller cross-compile to a static aarch64 binary. The full arm64 image is unverified, because the build machine has no qemu.\n- A v1.16 database migrates under v1.20. Only an empty one was tested.\n\n## Before deploying\n\n1. Create the signing key Secret once and keep it, because rotating it changes the spindle's identity:\n   ```bash\n   openssl ecparam -name prime256v1 -genkey -noout -out spindle-key.pem\n   kubectl create secret generic loom-spindle-key -n loom-system --from-file=spindle-key.pem=spindle-key.pem\n   ```\n   With Helm, set `spindle.signingKey.existingSecret=loom-spindle-key`.\n2. Set the contact email: `spindle.contactEmail` in Helm, or the TODO in `config/manager/manager.yaml`. The spindle won't start without it.\n3. Admission is `closed` by default: only the owner, `spindle.admins` and the allow-list get CI. v1.16 members aren't migrated.\n4. Hydrant shares the 1Gi spindle PVC; its growth is unknown.\n5. Back up `spindle.db` first.\n\nThe old `sh.tangled.*` routes are gone in v1.20.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"
          },
          "createdAt": "2026-11-21T18:09:12Z",
          "state": "open",
          "targetBranch": "main",
          "title": {
